我有一个关于加油站取景地的小花絮。

619
00:27:41.030 --> 00:27:42.710
Not a breakdown, a tidbit.
不是深度解析，只是个小花絮。

620
00:27:42.850 --> 00:27:43.550
It's a tidbit.
是个小花絮。

621
00:27:43.690 --> 00:27:45.330
It's a breakdown slash tidbit.
算是深度解析加小花絮吧。

622
00:27:45.470 --> 00:27:48.190
And then I also have a standards and practices name.
然后我还有一个关于审查部门的名字。

623
00:27:48.470 --> 00:27:50.110
Which one would you like first?
你想先听哪一个？

624
00:27:50.270 --> 00:27:51.770
Standards and practices, please.
先说审查部门的吧，请。

625
00:27:52.150 --> 00:27:52.590
All right.
好的。

626
00:27:52.770 --> 00:27:54.190
Fan question from Corey E.
来自科罗拉多州丹佛市的科里·E的粉丝提问。

627
00:27:54.310 --> 00:27:55.170
in Denver, Colorado.
他说：

628
00:27:55.530 --> 00:28:00.590
In re-watching this episode, I noticed that when Michael goes into the gas station, over
在重温这一集时，我注意到当迈克尔走进加油站时，在他肩膀

629
00:28:00.590 --> 00:28:04.730
his shoulder, there is a grasshopper lawn care sign behind him.
上方，背景里有一个“蚱蜢草坪护理”的招牌。

630
00:28:04.730 --> 00:28:08.570
That is my friend's Pennsylvania-based lawn care company.
那是我的朋友在宾夕法尼亚州经营的草坪护理公司。

631
00:28:08.650 --> 00:28:12.610
I asked her about it, and she said, you guys did a prop drop.
我问过她这件事，她说，你们当时做了道具植入。

632
00:28:12.930 --> 00:28:13.470
Oh.
哦。

633
00:28:13.790 --> 00:28:14.710
This is true.
这是真的。

634
00:28:15.170 --> 00:28:18.550
Phil Shea got this actual sign from a local company.
菲尔·谢伊从当地一家公司拿到了这个真实的招牌。

635
00:28:18.590 --> 00:28:23.610
He had it put up in the background of this scene to give it a kind of local credibility.
他把它挂在这一幕的背景里，为了增加一种当地的真实感。

636
00:28:23.610 --> 00:28:30.750
However, Randy said that originally the sign had the real phone number for the business.
然而，兰迪说最初这个招牌上印的是该企业的真实电话号码。

637
00:28:30.990 --> 00:28:36.390
It was like 1-800-LAWN-CARE, I think, and it is on the sign.
我想大概是1-800-LAWN-CARE之类的，招牌上确实有。

638
00:28:36.710 --> 00:28:39.530
And standards and practices flagged it.
然后审查部门把它标记出来了。

639
00:28:39.690 --> 00:28:43.830
They said this is not a cleared phone number, and you're going to have to digitally remove
他们说这不是一个获准使用的电话号码，你们必须在后期制作中

640
00:28:43.830 --> 00:28:44.830
it in post-production.
把它数字抹除掉。

641
00:28:45.190 --> 00:28:47.390
So much sass from them, always.
他们总是那么刻薄。

642
00:28:47.570 --> 00:28:47.990
I know.
我知道。

643
00:28:48.130 --> 00:28:51.930
But at least this time, they didn't have to type any curse words.
但至少这一次，他们不需要打任何脏话。

644
00:28:52.190 --> 00:28:52.290
Mm-mm.
嗯。

645
00:28:52.650 --> 00:28:53.970
I wonder if they were bummed.
我不知道他们会不会感到失望。

646
00:28:54.270 --> 00:28:57.110
I wonder if they were like, oh, just a sign.
不知道他们会不会觉得，哦，只是个招牌而已。

647
00:28:57.270 --> 00:29:03.010
Actually, I think that their email said, please digitally remove the f***ing phone number
其实，我觉得他们的邮件里写的是，请把招牌上那该死的电话号码

648
00:29:03.010 --> 00:29:03.850
from the sign.
数字抹除掉。

649
00:29:03.850 --> 00:29:05.090
It is not cleared.
它没有获准使用。

650
00:29:05.270 --> 00:29:06.750
As previously stated.
如前所述。

651
00:29:06.750 --> 00:29:07.510
Exactly.
没错。

652
00:29:08.450 --> 00:29:10.670
Please lose the f***ing phone number.
别再提那个该死的电话号码了。

653
00:29:11.330 --> 00:29:13.930
Here is your location tidbit.
这是给你们准备的拍摄地小花絮。

654
00:29:14.600 --> 00:29:18.110
We shot this at Civic Center Gas Station in Minimart.
我们是在范奈斯的一家市民中心加油站便利店拍的。

655
00:29:18.290 --> 00:29:19.290
It's in Van Nuys.
就在范奈斯。

656
00:29:19.690 --> 00:29:24.450
It is now closed, but their Yelp review page is still up.
现在已经关门了，但他们的Yelp评论页面还在。

657
00:29:24.670 --> 00:29:30.830
And it had one four-star review and three one-star reviews.
上面有一条四星评价和三条一星评价。

658
00:29:31.450 --> 00:29:32.850
Were they up the bathroom?
他们是在厕所里写的吗？

659
00:29:33.130 --> 00:29:35.490
Here is one of the one-star reviews.
这是其中一条一星评价。

660
00:29:35.690 --> 00:29:35.990
Okay.
好的。

661
00:29:36.550 --> 00:29:42.250
Quote, bathroom gets seven out of ten, mostly for a quiet, enjoyable time.
引用如下：厕所评分七分，满分十分，主要是因为那里安静，能享受一段愉快的时光。

662
00:29:42.730 --> 00:29:43.290
What?
什么？

663
00:29:43.470 --> 00:29:44.770
What are you doing getting there?
你跑那儿去干什么？

664
00:29:45.450 --> 00:29:49.750
My friend was banging on the door to get my attention, and I couldn't hear his thing.
我朋友当时在外面猛敲门想引起我注意，但我根本听不见他的动静。

665
00:29:49.770 --> 00:29:50.070
Oh, come on.
噢，得了吧。

666
00:29:50.250 --> 00:29:50.950
Come on.
别闹了。

667
00:29:50.990 --> 00:29:52.670
Made my experience peaceful.
让我的体验变得很宁静。

668
00:29:52.990 --> 00:29:55.530
The cashier is another story, though.
不过收银员又是另一回事了。

669
00:29:56.030 --> 00:30:02.530
Not only was he rude, suggested my friend abandoned me there, my best friend, but when I
他不仅态度粗鲁，还暗示我朋友把我抛弃在那儿了，那可是我最好的朋友，而且当我

670
00:30:02.530 --> 00:30:07.070
needed to use his phone, he didn't have any of my numbers on speed dial for me to call
需要借用他的电话时，他手机的快速拨号里根本没有我能打给

671
00:30:07.070 --> 00:30:07.590
a ride.
叫车的号码。

672
00:30:08.170 --> 00:30:11.970
Turns out my friend did leave me something about a baby emergency.
结果我朋友确实给我留了言，说是家里有急事。

673
00:30:12.730 --> 00:30:13.910
Who wrote that?
那是谁写的？

674
00:30:14.350 --> 00:30:16.930
Was it one of our writers, or was that a fan of the show?
是我们编剧写的，还是剧迷写的？

675
00:30:17.170 --> 00:30:18.510
No, it was just a fan of the show.
不，只是个剧迷写的。

676
00:30:18.650 --> 00:30:19.590
That's brilliant.
太天才了。

677
00:30:19.850 --> 00:30:20.570
Brilliant, right?
天才吧？

678
00:30:20.790 --> 00:30:21.150
Yes.
是的。

679
00:30:21.310 --> 00:30:22.950
I really liked that little tidbit.
我真的很喜欢这个小花絮。

680
00:30:22.950 --> 00:30:23.490
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

681
00:30:23.690 --> 00:30:24.390
That's awesome.
太棒了。

682
00:30:25.130 --> 00:30:27.610
Well, Michael's going to have a talking head where he says, you know what?
迈克尔会有一个单人访谈，他说，你知道吗？

683
00:30:27.670 --> 00:30:28.190
This is good.
这挺好的。

684
00:30:28.370 --> 00:30:32.630
I'm actually going to take this opportunity to go walkabout, and no cameras.
我正好趁这个机会去流浪，而且不带摄像机。

685
00:30:32.790 --> 00:30:35.010
He shoos the cameras away, which he never does.
他把摄像机赶走了，这可是他从没做过的事。

686
00:30:35.710 --> 00:30:38.150
There was a candy bag alt for this talking head.
这个访谈还有一个关于糖果袋的备选版本。

687
00:30:38.150 --> 00:30:39.210
Oh, please.
噢，拜托。

688
00:30:40.070 --> 00:30:41.650
This is what Michael says.
迈克尔是这么说的。

689
00:30:42.030 --> 00:30:45.390
This was not the day for one of your prank-a-roonies, Jim.
吉姆，今天可不是开你那些恶作剧玩笑的时候。

690
00:30:45.630 --> 00:30:47.290
I would have loved this yesterday.
要是昨天我肯定会很喜欢。

691
00:30:47.290 --> 00:30:49.470
I would have laughed my butt off.
我肯定会笑得前仰后合。

692
00:30:49.590 --> 00:30:50.390
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

693
00:30:50.570 --> 00:30:52.510
This is a blessing in the skies.
这真是因祸得福（blessing in the skies）。

694
00:30:52.990 --> 00:30:54.150
I'm going walkabout.
我要去流浪了。

695
00:30:54.930 --> 00:30:56.150
Blessing in the skies.
因祸得福。

696
00:30:56.230 --> 00:30:57.690
A blessing in the skies.
真是因祸得福。

697
00:30:57.810 --> 00:31:00.530
I really like it when Michael gets phrases wrong.
我真的很喜欢迈克尔说错成语的时候。

698
00:31:00.710 --> 00:31:02.630
I do, too, because I can relate.
我也是，因为我很有共鸣。

699
00:31:02.990 --> 00:31:05.190
I might have said blessing in the skies.
我也可能会说成“因祸得福（blessing in the skies）”。

700
00:31:06.710 --> 00:31:09.550
Back at the office, a search party is forming.
在办公室那边，搜寻队正在集结。

701
00:31:09.730 --> 00:31:14.490
It is going to consist of Holly, Aaron, and Dwight.
这组人将由霍莉、亚伦和德怀特组成。

702
00:31:15.010 --> 00:31:19.690
Yes, Dwight is going to say that he can't drive, though, because he's got a car full of fox meat.
是的，德怀特会说他没法开车，因为他的车里装满了狐狸肉。

703
00:31:20.330 --> 00:31:23.970
I can't even tell you how many alts they had for that line.
我甚至没法告诉你那句台词他们准备了多少个备选方案。

704
00:31:24.110 --> 00:31:25.130
For why he can't drive?
是因为他没法开车吗？

705
00:31:25.450 --> 00:31:27.090
Like two pages of alts.
大概有两页纸的备选方案。

706
00:31:27.150 --> 00:31:28.150
I'm not even kidding.
我真没开玩笑。

707
00:31:28.310 --> 00:31:28.930
I don't doubt it.
我对此深信不疑。

708
00:31:28.930 --> 00:31:31.710
I'm just going to give you three, because there were so many.
我只给你念三个，因为实在太多了。

709
00:31:31.850 --> 00:31:32.170
Okay.
好的。

710
00:31:32.510 --> 00:31:33.210
Here they were.
当时是这样的。

711
00:31:33.930 --> 00:31:34.750
You drive.
你来开车。

712
00:31:34.750 --> 00:31:36.430
I have a car full of scarecrow heads.
我的车里装满了稻草人头。

713
00:31:37.590 --> 00:31:38.910
You laugh out loud.
你大声笑了出来。

714
00:31:40.050 --> 00:31:40.450
You drive.
你来开车。

715
00:31:40.690 --> 00:31:41.830
I have a car full of pennies.
我的车里装满了硬币。

716
00:31:42.090 --> 00:31:44.710
Stupid bank only lets me convert $10,000 a day.
愚蠢的银行每天只让我兑换一万美元。

717
00:31:45.430 --> 00:31:46.090
You drive.
你来开车。

718
00:31:46.290 --> 00:31:48.190
I have a car full of Christmas ornaments I'm returning.
我的车里装满了我要去退货的圣诞装饰品。

719
00:31:48.470 --> 00:31:50.270
30 days, and I have the receipts.
才30天，而且我有收据。

720
00:31:51.150 --> 00:31:52.830
There were two pages of these.
这些备选方案足足有两页纸。

721
00:31:53.510 --> 00:31:54.470
I want more.
我还想听更多。

722
00:31:54.630 --> 00:31:55.610
I wish there were more.
我也希望还有更多。

723
00:31:55.770 --> 00:31:56.390
There were.
确实还有。

724
00:31:56.550 --> 00:31:59.470
I just didn't know if I would bore you guys if I just read a ton of them.
我只是不知道如果我读太多会不会让你们觉得无聊。

725
00:31:59.590 --> 00:32:00.570
They're very funny.
它们非常有趣。

726
00:32:01.250 --> 00:32:03.190
Well, listen, I think we should take a break.
好吧，听着，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

727
00:32:03.610 --> 00:32:06.150
When we come back, we're going to learn all about sticky quips.
回来之后，我们将深入了解什么是“粘性俏皮话”。

728
00:32:06.470 --> 00:32:07.430
Oh, yes.
噢，太棒了。

729
00:32:07.630 --> 00:32:10.490
And we're going to see who has the best instincts for finding Michael.
我们还要看看谁最有直觉能找到迈克尔。

730
00:32:19.200 --> 00:32:21.840
We're in the kitchen at eight minutes, five seconds.
我们在八分零五秒时来到了厨房。

731
00:32:22.100 --> 00:32:24.060
We get a nice shot of Pam's doodle.
我们得到了一个帕姆涂鸦的特写镜头。

732
00:32:24.680 --> 00:32:29.820
Randy shared with us that at this time, Henry Sane, our graphics designer, had left our show
兰迪告诉我们，当时我们的平面设计师亨利·塞恩已经离开了剧组，

733
00:32:29.820 --> 00:32:30.740
to direct a feature.
去执导一部长片了。

734
00:32:30.740 --> 00:32:32.360
We all loved Henry.
我们都很喜欢亨利。

735
00:32:32.560 --> 00:32:33.380
He was amazing.
他太棒了。

736
00:32:33.640 --> 00:32:38.500
But for this episode, we added a new member to our art department, Michael Bayeuth.
但对于这一集，我们美术部门增加了一位新成员，迈克尔·巴尤斯。

737
00:32:38.640 --> 00:32:41.240
And he would be our graphic artist for this episode.
他将担任这一集的平面设计师。

738
00:32:41.380 --> 00:32:43.440
So that is who designed this doodle.
所以这个涂鸦就是他设计的。

739
00:32:44.080 --> 00:32:50.380
Pam is very tickled because she notices that people have added captions to the bottom of
帕姆感到非常高兴，因为她注意到有人在她的涂鸦底部，

740
00:32:50.380 --> 00:32:50.980
her doodle.
加上了配文。

741
00:32:51.100 --> 00:32:51.420
Yeah.
是的。

742
00:32:51.620 --> 00:32:52.560
And they're quite funny.
而且它们非常有趣。

743
00:32:52.560 --> 00:32:57.200
So she's actually going to walk into the bullpen and say, guys, these are fun.
所以她真的会走进办公区说，伙计们，这些很有意思。

744
00:32:57.740 --> 00:32:58.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

745
00:32:58.480 --> 00:33:02.180
This starts a whole caption contest runner for the episode.
这开启了这一集里贯穿始终的配文比赛情节。

746
00:33:02.180 --> 00:33:04.380
And everyone really wants to get involved.
每个人都非常想参与进来。

747
00:33:04.560 --> 00:33:05.680
Especially Daryl.
尤其是达里尔。

748
00:33:06.020 --> 00:33:06.380
Yeah.
是的。

749
00:33:06.380 --> 00:33:11.180
Apparently, Daryl writes his own captions for Family Circus, and his daughter, like, cracks
显然，达里尔会为《家庭马戏团》漫画写自己的配文，而且他女儿，就，笑得，

750
00:33:11.180 --> 00:33:11.420
up.
前仰后合。

751
00:33:11.500 --> 00:33:12.400
He's really good at it.
他真的很擅长这个。

752
00:33:12.760 --> 00:33:15.440
I did a little mini deep dive on caption contests.
我专门对“配文大赛”做了一点小小的深度研究。

753
00:33:15.700 --> 00:33:16.980
Oh, I knew you would.
噢，我就知道你会这么做。

754
00:33:17.260 --> 00:33:23.540
So first of all, this episode of The Office appears on the Wikipedia page about caption
首先，这一集《办公室》出现在了维基百科关于“配文”的页面上，

755
00:33:23.540 --> 00:33:24.180
contests.
关于配文大赛的页面。

756
00:33:24.240 --> 00:33:24.740
Does it really?
真的吗？

757
00:33:24.740 --> 00:33:26.320
And the history of caption contests.
还有配文大赛的历史。

758
00:33:26.420 --> 00:33:26.760
Yes.
是的。

759
00:33:27.540 --> 00:33:33.620
So according to this Wikipedia page, the first printed caption contest seems to have appeared
根据这个维基百科页面，最早的印刷版配文大赛似乎出现在

760
00:33:33.620 --> 00:33:38.280
in Life magazine, which ran from 1883 to 1936.
《生活》杂志上，该杂志从1883年发行到1936年。

761
00:33:38.980 --> 00:33:41.140
But this was fascinating to me.
但这对我来说太有意思了。

762
00:33:41.420 --> 00:33:44.200
They were not called caption contests.
它们当时不叫配文大赛。

763
00:33:44.580 --> 00:33:49.980
They were called picture title contests or picture headline contests.
它们被称为“图片标题大赛”或“图片头条大赛”。

764
00:33:50.660 --> 00:33:51.920
And here's why.
原因如下。

765
00:33:52.120 --> 00:33:52.420
Why?
为什么？

766
00:33:52.760 --> 00:33:55.220
The word caption didn't exiSt.
因为当时还没有“caption”（配文）这个词。

767
00:33:55.460 --> 00:33:55.980
Come on.
别逗了。

768
00:33:56.120 --> 00:33:56.940
It didn't.
真的没有。

769
00:33:57.040 --> 00:33:58.380
Who invented the word caption?
是谁发明了“caption”这个词？

770
00:33:58.660 --> 00:34:02.420
I don't know, but it did not show up in the English language until the first half of
我不知道，但它直到20世纪上半叶才出现在英语语言中。

771
00:34:02.420 --> 00:34:03.280
the 20th century.
20世纪。

772
00:34:03.620 --> 00:34:04.000
Huh.
哈。

773
00:34:04.400 --> 00:34:07.720
Now you go on Instagram, people post a photo and say, caption this.
现在你上Instagram，人们发照片时会说“给这张图配个文”。

774
00:34:07.880 --> 00:34:08.140
Yeah.
是啊。

775
00:34:08.360 --> 00:34:10.540
You better be careful when you write that sometimes.
有时候写这个词你最好小心点。

776
00:34:11.840 --> 00:34:13.100
Well, that is true.
嗯，确实如此。

777
00:34:13.920 --> 00:34:16.500
And I've got a little fun fact as well.
我也有个有趣的小知识。

778
00:34:16.660 --> 00:34:16.880
Okay.
好啊。

779
00:34:17.620 --> 00:34:21.520
OfficeTally.com ran a caption contest after this episode aired.
OfficeTally.com在这一集播出后举办了一场配文大赛。

780
00:34:21.700 --> 00:34:25.920
They put up the drawing of the Sabre printer, and people could submit captions.
他们贴出了那台Sabre打印机的图，让人们提交配文。

781
00:34:26.480 --> 00:34:28.480
And here were a couple that I thought were fun.
我觉得其中有几个挺有趣的。

782
00:34:28.600 --> 00:34:29.420
Was there a winner?
有获胜者吗？

783
00:34:29.720 --> 00:34:30.420
There was.
有的。

784
00:34:30.420 --> 00:34:32.900
And the winner got a prize package.
获胜者还得到了一个奖品包。

785
00:34:32.900 --> 00:34:40.120
They got a DVD, The Office Overtime, a Creed Thoughts shirt, and a Dunder Mifflin coffee
他们得到了一张DVD、《办公室》花絮、一件Creed Thoughts衬衫，还有一个Dunder Mifflin咖啡

786
00:34:40.120 --> 00:34:40.500
tumbler.
随行杯。

787
00:34:40.520 --> 00:34:41.240
So fun.
太棒了。

788
00:34:41.400 --> 00:34:41.600
Right?
对吧？

789
00:34:41.800 --> 00:34:42.560
Let's hear some.
让我们听听看。

790
00:34:42.840 --> 00:34:43.080
Okay.
好的。

791
00:34:43.220 --> 00:34:50.120
So the contest page is down, but some people had also submitted their captions in the comments,
虽然比赛页面已经撤下了，但有些人还在评论区提交了他们的配文，

792
00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:51.300
which are still up.
那些评论还在。

793
00:34:52.100 --> 00:34:56.480
Brick wrote, quote, I work so hard so my son can become a scanner.
Brick写道：“我工作如此努力，就是为了让我儿子能成为一台扫描仪。”

794
00:34:57.420 --> 00:34:58.400
That was one.
这是其中一个。

795
00:34:58.400 --> 00:35:02.620
And then Jordan went with, hey, look over here.
然后Jordan写的是：“嘿，看这边。”

796
00:35:02.620 --> 00:35:04.860
I'm just about as white and square as Gabe.
“我长得跟Gabe一样又白又方。”

797
00:35:05.600 --> 00:35:09.260
So he really went in the direction of the episode.
所以他确实是朝着这一集的方向去写的。

798
00:35:10.960 --> 00:35:13.220
Dwight, Holly, and Erin are searching for Michael.
Dwight、Holly和Erin正在寻找Michael。

799
00:35:13.380 --> 00:35:14.780
They start with the gas station.
他们从加油站开始找起。

800
00:35:14.980 --> 00:35:18.520
They ask the gas station attendant which way Michael went.
他们问加油站员工Michael往哪个方向走了。

801
00:35:18.760 --> 00:35:22.520
And as it turns out, it's exactly where Holly would have gone.
结果证明，那正是霍莉会去的地方。

802
00:35:22.700 --> 00:35:27.000
She had predicted that he might have gone in the direction of the bakery just for the smell.
她预料到他可能会因为闻到香味而往面包店的方向走。

803
00:35:27.560 --> 00:35:29.040
And that's the way he went.
而他确实往那边去了。

804
00:35:30.020 --> 00:35:30.180
Yeah.
没错。

805
00:35:30.600 --> 00:35:37.720
At 9 minutes and 37 seconds, you see this sign for a bakery, the thing that Holly sees.
在9分37秒时，你可以看到那个面包店的招牌，也就是霍莉看到的东西。

806
00:35:37.860 --> 00:35:38.760
That was a fake bakery.
那是一家假的面包店。

807
00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:39.660
It doesn't exiSt.
它根本不存在。

808
00:35:39.800 --> 00:35:40.640
We made that sign.
那个招牌是我们做的。

809
00:35:41.080 --> 00:35:46.600
And I guess past the bakery, Michael's going to wander into a pet store where he's going
我想过了面包店，迈克尔会溜进一家宠物店，在那里他会

810
00:35:46.600 --> 00:35:48.220
to start talking to the animals.
开始和动物们说话。

811
00:35:48.900 --> 00:35:53.180
This was a real pet store on Victory Boulevard in Burbank, California.
这是一家位于加利福尼亚州伯班克市胜利大道的真实宠物店。

812
00:35:53.180 --> 00:35:57.160
It was filled with animals, but we didn't use their animals.
店里满是动物，但我们没有用他们的动物。

813
00:35:57.160 --> 00:35:59.040
We brought in our own animals.
我们带了自己的动物来。

814
00:35:59.240 --> 00:36:02.240
They were provided by Bob Dunn's Animal Services.
它们是由鲍勃·邓恩动物服务公司提供的。

815
00:36:02.740 --> 00:36:04.600
You know, we used them all the time.
你知道的，我们一直都在用他们。

816
00:36:04.800 --> 00:36:06.740
Our head trainer was Denise Sanders.
我们的首席训练师是丹妮丝·桑德斯。

817
00:36:07.300 --> 00:36:10.780
Randy sent us the photos of the puppies that they caSt.
兰迪把他们选中的小狗照片发给了我们。

818
00:36:11.080 --> 00:36:12.040
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

819
00:36:12.040 --> 00:36:12.920
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

820
00:36:13.080 --> 00:36:15.100
We have all the pictures of these little dogs.
我们有所有这些小狗的照片。

821
00:36:15.420 --> 00:36:16.580
That's the job I want.
那才是我想要的工作。

822
00:36:16.700 --> 00:36:22.520
I want the job where I look through the puppy pictures and I pick puppies for a day of work.
我想要那种整天翻看小狗照片，然后挑选小狗去工作一天的工作。

823
00:36:23.180 --> 00:36:27.860
We don't know the names of the tiny golden retrievers, but the Yorkie was played by Amos.
我们不知道那些小金毛的名字，但那只约克夏犬是由阿莫斯扮演的。

824
00:36:28.240 --> 00:36:30.980
Michael talks to a macaw who was named Hook.
迈克尔和一只名叫胡克的金刚鹦鹉说话。

825
00:36:31.580 --> 00:36:32.980
He talks to a snake.
他还和一条蛇说话。

826
00:36:33.100 --> 00:36:34.080
We don't know the snake's name.
我们不知道那条蛇的名字。

827
00:36:34.200 --> 00:36:34.660
Sorry, guys.
抱歉啦，各位。

828
00:36:35.080 --> 00:36:39.060
And we used two puppies to play the, quote, licking puppy.
我们用了两只小狗来扮演那只“舔人”的小狗。

829
00:36:39.280 --> 00:36:40.400
They were very cute.
它们非常可爱。

830
00:36:40.700 --> 00:36:43.080
You know, we got a fan question from Natasha C.
我们收到了来自德克萨斯州达拉斯市娜塔莎·C的一位粉丝提问。

831
00:36:43.180 --> 00:36:43.980
in Dallas, Texas.
在德克萨斯州达拉斯市。

832
00:36:43.980 --> 00:36:48.160
When Michael was in the pet store holding the puppy, the puppy licks his nose.
当迈克尔在宠物店抱着小狗时，小狗舔了他的鼻子。

833
00:36:48.440 --> 00:36:53.360
Was the puppy trained to do this or was this just perfect timing and improv on Michael's part?
那是训练出来的，还是纯属巧合，或者是迈克尔的即兴发挥？

834
00:36:53.820 --> 00:36:55.620
I'll tell you what, Natasha.
我来告诉你吧，娜塔莎。

835
00:36:56.000 --> 00:36:58.400
All of the little pet store vignettes were scripted.
所有宠物店的小片段都是写好的剧本。

836
00:36:58.540 --> 00:37:00.360
They sound so off the cuff.
它们听起来那么随性。

837
00:37:00.540 --> 00:37:06.440
But everything, the things he says to the snake, the thing he says to the macaw, all scripted,
但所有的一切，他对蛇说的话，对金刚鹦鹉说的话，全都是剧本写好的，

838
00:37:06.440 --> 00:37:10.020
included, including the part where the puppy was supposed to lick his nose.
包括小狗舔他鼻子的那一部分。

839
00:37:10.220 --> 00:37:14.780
The puppy licks his nose exactly in the spot it's supposed to.
小狗舔他鼻子的位置分毫不差。

840
00:37:14.860 --> 00:37:16.260
I don't know how they did it.
我不知道他们是怎么做到的。

841
00:37:16.260 --> 00:37:17.280
How did they pull that off?
他们是怎么搞定这一点的？

842
00:37:17.280 --> 00:37:19.760
I don't know because it's not supposed to lick him at firSt.
我不知道，因为按理说它起初不该舔他。

843
00:37:19.760 --> 00:37:21.260
It's supposed to lick him in the middle.
它应该在中间的时候舔他。

844
00:37:21.660 --> 00:37:22.620
All scripted.
全是剧本安排的。

845
00:37:22.960 --> 00:37:28.140
And Steve did such a great job of making that just feel like 100% spontaneous.
史蒂夫做得太棒了，让这一切看起来百分之百自然随性。

846
00:37:28.340 --> 00:37:28.620
I know.
我知道。

847
00:37:28.760 --> 00:37:29.180
All of it.
全部都是。

848
00:37:29.520 --> 00:37:33.300
Back at the office, Pam was like, well, if I knew you guys loved caption contests,
回到办公室，帕姆说，好吧，如果我知道你们这么喜欢看图配文大赛，

849
00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:35.860
I would have drawn something different that you could really have fun with.
我就画点别的，让你们能玩得更开心了。

850
00:37:35.900 --> 00:37:36.920
And so she does.
于是她就这么做了。

851
00:37:37.220 --> 00:37:41.660
She draws two large dogs on an island with two palm trees.
她在岛上画了两只大狗，还有两棵棕榈树。

852
00:37:42.000 --> 00:37:46.440
But before anybody can give their captions, Gabe kind of shuts it down.
但在大家给出标题之前，盖博就把这事儿给叫停了。

853
00:37:46.740 --> 00:37:48.480
Yeah, he's a total fun stopper.
没错，他简直是个扫兴鬼。

854
00:37:48.960 --> 00:37:52.560
He says they can do it if they can agree on some ground rules.
他说如果大家能商定一些基本规则，就可以继续。

855
00:37:52.760 --> 00:37:55.060
Number one, no insulting the company.
第一，不许侮辱公司。

856
00:37:55.360 --> 00:37:57.640
Number two, no pop culture references.
第二，不许引用流行文化。

857
00:37:58.320 --> 00:38:02.860
And finally, they have to write their captions on Dunder Mifflin's sabers.
最后，他们必须把标题写在邓德·米夫林的“妙语贴”上。

858
00:38:03.300 --> 00:38:04.360
Sticky quips.
妙语贴。

859
00:38:04.660 --> 00:38:05.180
Yes.
没错。

860
00:38:05.460 --> 00:38:06.840
And then Gabe has a talking head.
然后盖博有个采访镜头。

861
00:38:07.000 --> 00:38:08.640
He says, sticky quips are fun.
他说，妙语贴很有趣。

862
00:38:08.820 --> 00:38:09.340
They're safe.
它们很安全。

863
00:38:09.520 --> 00:38:10.040
They're handy.
它们很方便。

864
00:38:10.320 --> 00:38:14.580
I like to use sticky quips as regular post-it notes when I'm in a fun mood.
我心情好的时候，喜欢把妙语贴当成普通的便利贴用。

865
00:38:14.820 --> 00:38:15.800
Not every day.
不是每天都用。

866
00:38:16.240 --> 00:38:19.560
There was an alt for this talking head where Gabe simply just said,
这个采访镜头有个备选版本，盖博当时只是简单地说：

867
00:38:19.700 --> 00:38:21.920
I don't have a lot of responsibility here.
我在这里没什么责任。

868
00:38:22.360 --> 00:38:24.600
Oh, wow.
哇哦。

869
00:38:26.180 --> 00:38:28.520
We had a fan question from Joshua P.
我们收到了一位来自辛辛那提的粉丝Joshua P.的提问。

870
00:38:28.800 --> 00:38:29.500
in Cincinnati.
辛辛那提的。

871
00:38:29.500 --> 00:38:35.180
Did sticky quips already exist out there somewhere or did Phil Shea have to find a way to create them?
妙语贴是本来就有的，还是菲尔·谢专门想办法制作出来的？

872
00:38:35.500 --> 00:38:37.320
Well, Joshua, they did not exiSt.
嗯，Joshua，它们本来是不存在的。

873
00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:39.920
Let's give you a visual of a sticky quip.
让我们来看看妙语贴长什么样。

874
00:38:40.060 --> 00:38:43.680
It's basically a post-it note, but it's shaped like a speech bubble.
它基本上就是个便利贴，但形状像个对话气泡。

875
00:38:43.680 --> 00:38:44.660
Like an idea bubble.
就像个想法气泡一样。

876
00:38:44.820 --> 00:38:45.020
Yeah.
没错。

877
00:38:45.300 --> 00:38:50.680
And Phil Shea had to design them, and he used Earl Hay Press to manufacture and package them.
菲尔·谢必须设计它们，并找了厄尔·海印刷公司来制造和包装。

878
00:38:50.880 --> 00:38:53.520
But I found what I'm calling a Reddit catch.
但我发现了一个我称之为“Reddit发现”的东西。

879
00:38:53.660 --> 00:38:53.920
Oh.
哦。

880
00:38:54.360 --> 00:38:58.160
When I googled sticky quips, I found this catch on Reddit.
当我谷歌搜索“妙语贴”时，我在Reddit上发现了这个发现。

881
00:38:58.480 --> 00:38:59.680
It's pretty fantastic.
真是太棒了。

882
00:38:59.900 --> 00:39:00.500
Let's hear it.
说来听听。

883
00:39:00.500 --> 00:39:08.960
It says, at 15 minutes and 32 seconds, in the pilot episode of The Office, Jim has a doodle taped to his computer monitor.
上面说，在《办公室》试播集15分32秒的时候，吉姆的电脑显示器上贴着一个涂鸦。

884
00:39:08.960 --> 00:39:12.460
It's while he's eating some Jell-O.
就在他吃果冻的时候。

885
00:39:12.680 --> 00:39:12.920
Okay.
好的。

886
00:39:13.380 --> 00:39:19.640
And there are four mini sticky notes with word bubbles drawn on them with captions inside.
上面有四个迷你便利贴，画着对话气泡，里面写着标题。

887
00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:28.320
So someone has captioned this doodle, or four people have captioned this doodle, using sort of the original sticky quip.
所以有人给这个涂鸦写了标题，或者说有四个人给这个涂鸦写了标题，用的是某种原始版的妙语贴。

888
00:39:28.540 --> 00:39:28.900
Huh.
哈。

889
00:39:29.140 --> 00:39:30.060
It was kind of cool.
这挺酷的。

890
00:39:30.060 --> 00:39:30.520
Yeah.
确实。

891
00:39:31.340 --> 00:39:35.440
Well, we asked Brent about the name Sticky Quips, and this is what he had to say.
我们问了布伦特关于“妙语贴”这个名字的由来，他是这么说的。

892
00:39:35.620 --> 00:39:40.660
He said, that's just one of those two-word phrases that comedy writers love.
他说，这只是喜剧编剧喜欢的那种双词短语。

893
00:39:40.780 --> 00:39:47.740
It's got multiple K sounds, plus a T and a P, five plosives in two words.
它有多个K音，加上一个T和一个P，两个词里有五个爆破音。

894
00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:49.560
That's comedy power, people.
这就是喜剧的力量，各位。

895
00:39:50.200 --> 00:39:54.720
Angela, could you write a good caption for a picture?
安吉拉，你能给一张图片写出好的标题吗？

896
00:39:54.900 --> 00:39:55.700
Because I could not.
因为我写不出来。

897
00:39:55.860 --> 00:39:57.140
I just am not that clever.
我没那么聪明。

898
00:39:57.460 --> 00:39:58.660
I do enjoy it.
我倒是挺喜欢的。

899
00:39:58.880 --> 00:39:59.200
Really?
真的吗？

900
00:39:59.200 --> 00:39:59.560
I like it.
我喜欢。

901
00:39:59.660 --> 00:39:59.860
Yes.
是的。

902
00:39:59.860 --> 00:40:01.580
And they often do it at school.
而且他们经常在学校里做这件事。

903
00:40:01.760 --> 00:40:03.460
You know, our son is in sixth grade.
你知道，我儿子上六年级。

904
00:40:03.640 --> 00:40:06.160
They do a caption contest, and he won one week.
他们会举办看图写话比赛，他有一周还赢了。

905
00:40:06.340 --> 00:40:06.660
Really?
真的吗？

906
00:40:06.840 --> 00:40:07.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

907
00:40:07.220 --> 00:40:08.140
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

908
00:40:08.380 --> 00:40:09.920
I'm very impressed by that.
我对此印象非常深刻。

909
00:40:10.100 --> 00:40:14.460
I think maybe that is the same thing that would hold me back as an improviser.
我觉得这可能也是阻碍我成为即兴表演者的原因。

910
00:40:14.580 --> 00:40:16.120
I just get in my head about it.
我总是想得太多。

911
00:40:16.180 --> 00:40:16.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

912
00:40:16.400 --> 00:40:19.000
And I can't, it doesn't flow for me.
我做不到，感觉不顺畅。

913
00:40:19.640 --> 00:40:21.460
Oh, I love a good caption conteSt.
噢，我超爱看图写话比赛。

914
00:40:21.560 --> 00:40:22.860
Well, you're an improv person.
好吧，你是个即兴表演者。

915
00:40:23.000 --> 00:40:24.920
I feel like that makes so much sense.
我觉得这太合理了。

916
00:40:25.580 --> 00:40:26.500
Michael's getting hungry.
迈克尔饿了。

917
00:40:26.660 --> 00:40:31.420
He's going to stop at a hot dog stand, but he doesn't have any money, so he offers his watch.
他打算在热狗摊停下来，但他没带钱，于是他提出用手表抵押。

918
00:40:31.720 --> 00:40:33.000
The hot dog guy says no.
卖热狗的人拒绝了。

919
00:40:33.140 --> 00:40:35.680
Michael's like, well, what do you do with the unsold hot dogs?
迈克尔就问，那你们卖不掉的热狗怎么办？

920
00:40:35.680 --> 00:40:40.160
And the guy says they throw them away at the end of the day, and Michael's like, why don't you throw one into my mouth?
那人说每天结束时都会扔掉，迈克尔就说，那你为什么不直接扔一个进我嘴里呢？

921
00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:41.280
Right.
没错。

922
00:40:42.840 --> 00:40:44.460
I loved the hot dog guy.
我很喜欢那个卖热狗的人。

923
00:40:44.740 --> 00:40:46.040
Yeah, he was fantastic.
是啊，他太棒了。

924
00:40:46.420 --> 00:40:52.660
He was played by Chris Danuzio, and he's been on The Mentalist, New Girl, Law & Order.
他由克里斯·达努齐奥饰演，他曾出演过《超感神探》、《杰茜驾到》和《法律与秩序》。

925
00:40:52.840 --> 00:40:56.520
But I stumbled across his bio and listened to this.
但我偶然发现了他的简介，听听这个。

926
00:40:57.120 --> 00:41:05.380
Quote, after graduating Princeton with a bachelor's degree in history, Chris had a brief stint in the NFL with the Buffalo Bills.
引用一下：从普林斯顿大学历史系毕业后，克里斯曾在布法罗比尔队短暂效力于NFL。

927
00:41:05.680 --> 00:41:05.900
What?
什么？

928
00:41:06.120 --> 00:41:08.960
Then he moved into the investment banking world.
然后他进入了投资银行界。

929
00:41:08.960 --> 00:41:13.480
And during this time, he also embarked on an acting and writing career.
在此期间，他还开启了演艺和写作生涯。

930
00:41:14.060 --> 00:41:16.000
Such, like, a diverse background.
背景真是太丰富了。

931
00:41:16.280 --> 00:41:16.820
I know.
我知道。

932
00:41:17.000 --> 00:41:20.780
History degree, NFL, investment banking, actor.
历史学位、NFL、投资银行、演员。

933
00:41:21.480 --> 00:41:23.440
I feel like you've covered all of it.
我觉得你把所有领域都涵盖了。

934
00:41:23.560 --> 00:41:23.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

935
00:41:24.400 --> 00:41:27.420
Here's a little location breakdown for you of the hot dog stand.
这是为你准备的热狗摊地点详细信息。

936
00:41:27.420 --> 00:41:30.260
It is a real place called Larry's Chili Dog.
那是一个真实存在的地方，叫“拉里辣椒热狗”。

937
00:41:30.520 --> 00:41:33.480
It is on Burbank Boulevard in Burbank, California.
它位于加利福尼亚州伯班克的伯班克大道上。

938
00:41:33.800 --> 00:41:36.320
It has 4.5 stars on Yelp.
它在Yelp上有4.5星的评价。

939
00:41:36.320 --> 00:41:37.840
It is open from 7 a.m.
营业时间从早上7点开始。

940
00:41:37.900 --> 00:41:38.860
to 3 p.m.
到下午3点结束。

941
00:41:38.940 --> 00:41:40.540
They also serve breakfaSt.
他们也供应早餐。

942
00:41:41.180 --> 00:41:47.040
I looked at the menu, and here are some of the hot dogs you can get at Larry's Chili Dog.
我看了菜单，以下是你在“拉里辣椒热狗”可以买到的一些热狗。

943
00:41:47.200 --> 00:41:48.040
For breakfast?
早餐也能吃？

944
00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:50.220
You can get them from 7 a.m.
你可以从早上7点开始买。

945
00:41:50.240 --> 00:41:50.960
to 3 p.m.
一直到下午3点。

946
00:41:51.060 --> 00:41:51.340
Okay.
好吧。

947
00:41:51.620 --> 00:41:52.980
They also have breakfast burritos.
他们也有早餐卷饼。

948
00:41:52.980 --> 00:41:54.260
They have breakfast food.
他们有早餐食品。

949
00:41:54.260 --> 00:41:57.240
But if you want one of their hot dogs for dinner, you're out of luck.
但如果你想晚餐吃他们的热狗，那你就没口福了。

950
00:41:57.660 --> 00:41:59.220
But here's what you can have.
不过，这是你可以享用的东西。

951
00:41:59.800 --> 00:42:00.940
A chili dog.
辣椒热狗。

952
00:42:01.100 --> 00:42:01.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

953
00:42:01.500 --> 00:42:02.200
A corn dog.
玉米热狗。

954
00:42:02.440 --> 00:42:03.440
A veggie dog.
素食热狗。

955
00:42:03.620 --> 00:42:05.800
Just a regular hot dog if you want.
如果你想的话，也可以选普通热狗。

956
00:42:05.960 --> 00:42:11.560
But then you can get the New York dog, which comes with grilled onion sauce and spicy mustard.
但你也可以选纽约热狗，配有烤洋葱酱和辣芥末酱。

957
00:42:12.080 --> 00:42:21.420
You can also get a Chicago dog, which includes green relish, mustard, tomatoes, onions, celery, salt, dill pickles, and spicy peppers.
你还可以选芝加哥热狗，里面有绿色腌菜、芥末、番茄、洋葱、芹菜、盐、莳萝酸黄瓜和辣味辣椒。

958
00:42:22.040 --> 00:42:22.400
Gross.
恶心。

959
00:42:22.720 --> 00:42:24.140
Chicago, what are you doing?
芝加哥，你们在搞什么？

960
00:42:24.380 --> 00:42:25.040
What's happening?
这是怎么回事？

961
00:42:25.120 --> 00:42:25.400
Settle down.
淡定点。

962
00:42:25.720 --> 00:42:26.940
Chicago, what's going on?
芝加哥，到底怎么了？

963
00:42:27.200 --> 00:42:28.880
Would you like a Reuben dog?
你想来个鲁宾热狗吗？

964
00:42:29.600 --> 00:42:35.760
Because that comes with sauerkraut, Russian dressing, and melted Swiss cheese and spicy mustard.
因为那个配有德国酸菜、俄罗斯酱、融化的瑞士芝士和辣芥末酱。

965
00:42:36.020 --> 00:42:37.000
Oh, my Lord.
天哪。

966
00:42:37.240 --> 00:42:39.780
I mean, it's worse than the Chicago dog.
我是说，这比芝加哥热狗还糟糕。

967
00:42:40.020 --> 00:42:42.180
And finally, the Hawaiian dog.
最后是夏威夷热狗。

968
00:42:42.360 --> 00:42:43.360
Does it have pineapple?
里面有菠萝吗？

969
00:42:43.640 --> 00:42:44.160
It does.
有的。

970
00:42:44.420 --> 00:42:46.440
Grilled pineapples, onions, and barbecue sauce.
烤菠萝、洋葱和烧烤酱。

971
00:42:46.680 --> 00:42:47.480
I'm intrigued.
我很有兴趣。

972
00:42:47.680 --> 00:42:48.600
I might try that one.
我可能会试试那个。

973
00:42:48.880 --> 00:42:50.100
But here's the kicker.
但重点来了。

974
00:42:50.100 --> 00:42:53.860
You can also get a puppy patty if you bring your dog.
如果你带了狗来，还可以买一份小狗肉饼。

975
00:42:54.080 --> 00:42:57.380
They'll give you a little beef patty for your dog.
他们会给你家狗狗一块小牛肉饼。

976
00:42:57.420 --> 00:42:58.960
And they serve Starbucks coffee.
而且他们还供应星巴克咖啡。

977
00:42:59.160 --> 00:43:00.700
I don't know how, but they do.
我不知道他们是怎么做到的，但确实有。

978
00:43:00.900 --> 00:43:05.660
Well, put this on your tour of Dunder Mifflin sites, guys, if you come out this way.
好吧，伙计们，如果你们来这边玩，记得把这儿加进你们的邓德·米夫林公司打卡之旅里。

979
00:43:05.820 --> 00:43:06.140
Yeah.
没错。

980
00:43:06.360 --> 00:43:09.000
Go get a hot dog at Larry's Chili Dog in Burbank.
去伯班克的拉里辣椒热狗店吃个热狗吧。

981
00:43:09.900 --> 00:43:14.800
Michael's going to move on because he sees a huge banner advertising a giant egg roll.
迈克尔继续往前走，因为他看到一个巨大的横幅，上面在宣传巨型春卷。

982
00:43:14.800 --> 00:43:15.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

983
00:43:15.540 --> 00:43:16.520
This catches his eye.
这吸引了他的目光。

984
00:43:16.720 --> 00:43:20.240
I'll let you know, these two spots were miles away from each other.
我得告诉你们，这两个地方离得有几英里远。

985
00:43:20.340 --> 00:43:23.220
There was no way that he could actually walk between these two places.
他根本不可能步行往返于这两个地方之间。

986
00:43:23.620 --> 00:43:25.800
Dwight, Erin, and Holly are still searching for Michael.
德怀特、艾琳和霍莉还在寻找迈克尔。

987
00:43:26.200 --> 00:43:27.920
Now we're at a grocery store with them.
现在我们和他们一起在一家杂货店。

988
00:43:28.020 --> 00:43:32.720
Dwight comes out, and Holly, I guess, is signing up for a new cell phone plan at a little kiosk,
德怀特出来了，而霍莉，我猜，正在一个小摊位前办理新的手机套餐，

989
00:43:32.760 --> 00:43:34.460
like a pop-up tent in the parking lot.
就像停车场里的一个临时帐篷。

990
00:43:34.460 --> 00:43:39.020
Yeah, she's really only doing it because she wants to get the little stress ball.
没错，她其实只是为了那个小解压球才去办的。

991
00:43:39.260 --> 00:43:44.460
I guess they're giving away free stress balls because she's given a fake name, Fanny Smellmore.
我猜他们是在免费赠送解压球，因为她报了一个假名，叫“芬妮·斯梅尔莫”。

992
00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:49.660
And the cell phone lady is like, wow, you must be friends with Orville Tootenbacher.
然后手机店的女士就说，哇，你一定是奥维尔·图滕巴赫的朋友吧。

993
00:43:50.060 --> 00:43:51.780
These two are so meant for each other.
这两人真是天生一对。

994
00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:52.260
Yeah.
没错。

995
00:43:52.640 --> 00:43:56.000
Orville Tootenbacher is Michael's millionaire character who farts popcorn.
奥维尔·图滕巴赫是迈克尔虚构的百万富翁角色，会放爆米花味的屁。

996
00:43:56.940 --> 00:43:59.340
Dwight and Erin know immediately that Michael's been there.
德怀特和艾琳立刻意识到迈克尔来过这里。

997
00:43:59.760 --> 00:44:04.280
Dwight starts to realize that Holly might just be the key to finding Michael.
德怀特开始意识到，霍莉可能就是找到迈克尔的关键。

998
00:44:04.460 --> 00:44:06.960
Because the two of them think just alike.
因为他们俩的想法如出一辙。

999
00:44:07.560 --> 00:44:08.040
Yes.
是的。

1000
00:44:08.260 --> 00:44:10.760
So they're going to ask Holly, where did he go next?
所以他们打算问霍莉，他接下来去了哪里？

1001
00:44:10.920 --> 00:44:11.300
Where?
在哪儿？

1002
00:44:11.860 --> 00:44:18.280
And Holly sees the same giant egg roll sign and says, are their egg rolls really that big?
霍莉看到了那个巨大的蛋卷招牌，问道，他们的蛋卷真的有那么大吗？

1003
00:44:18.660 --> 00:44:21.800
She's going to wander over there, and Dwight and Erin follow her.
她走过去逛了逛，德怀特和艾琳跟在她后面。

1004
00:44:22.160 --> 00:44:28.560
Before we leave this scene, I do want to give a shout out to our guest star who played the cell phone lady, Amy Hite.
在离开这个场景之前，我想向饰演手机女士的客串明星艾米·海特致敬。

1005
00:44:28.680 --> 00:44:30.360
She has a couple of office connections.
她和《办公室》有几层关系。

1006
00:44:30.890 --> 00:44:34.820
She was in Hello, Ladies with Stephen Merchant and Rutherford Falls with Ed HelMs.
她曾与斯蒂芬·莫昌特合作过《你好，女士》，还与艾德·赫尔姆斯合作过《卢瑟福瀑布》。

1007
00:44:34.900 --> 00:44:35.460
Look at that.
看那个。

1008
00:44:35.500 --> 00:44:36.280
She was great.
她演得太棒了。

1009
00:44:36.440 --> 00:44:37.120
I love it.
我喜欢。

1010
00:44:37.760 --> 00:44:40.560
They just miss Michael at the Chinese restaurant.
他们刚好错过了在中餐馆的迈克尔。

1011
00:44:40.560 --> 00:44:45.480
He's just finishing up his food, and he's going to have to do a dine and dash, or at least he tries to.
他刚吃完饭，打算吃霸王餐，或者说他尝试了。

1012
00:44:45.900 --> 00:44:47.980
Yeah, he's too honest for that.
是啊，他太老实了，做不出那种事。

1013
00:44:48.080 --> 00:44:48.560
I know.
我知道。

1014
00:44:48.560 --> 00:44:51.080
And he thinks he should get some points for that honesty.
而且他觉得这种诚实应该给他加分。

1015
00:44:51.340 --> 00:44:54.240
They're like, no, you tried to steal food.
他们却说，不，你这是试图偷吃东西。

1016
00:44:54.480 --> 00:44:56.580
And he ate a lot of food.
而且他吃了很多东西。

1017
00:44:56.720 --> 00:44:57.580
The number three.
第三点。

1018
00:44:58.500 --> 00:45:00.640
We had a fan question from Bennett H.
我们收到了一位粉丝贝内特·H的提问。

1019
00:45:00.740 --> 00:45:01.800
in Salt Lake City, Utah.
来自犹他州盐湖城。

1020
00:45:02.100 --> 00:45:07.320
Was the Chinese restaurant where Michael tried to dine and dash a real restaurant, and if so, which one?
迈克尔试图吃霸王餐的那家中餐馆是真实的餐厅吗？如果是，是哪一家？

1021
00:45:07.980 --> 00:45:09.740
Yes, it was a real restaurant.
是的，那是一家真实的餐厅。

1022
00:45:09.740 --> 00:45:10.720
It still exists.
它现在还开着。

1023
00:45:11.040 --> 00:45:16.960
In the show, we called it Mr. Chu's Chinese Food Restaurant, but it is actually Kung Pao China Bistro.
在剧中，我们叫它“朱先生中餐馆”，但它实际上叫“宫保中国小酒馆”。

1024
00:45:17.180 --> 00:45:22.300
It is on Ventura Boulevard in Studio City, California, although it is now called Mr. O's.
它位于加利福尼亚州影城的文图拉大道上，虽然现在改名叫“O先生”了。

1025
00:45:22.300 --> 00:45:26.060
Do you remember back when we did the christening episode?
还记得我们拍洗礼那一集的时候吗？

1026
00:45:26.360 --> 00:45:29.360
I told you about the woman who has a blog.
我跟你提过那个写博客的女人。

1027
00:45:29.620 --> 00:45:34.260
It's called I Am Not a Stalker, and she visits locations from TV shows and movies.
博客名叫“我不是跟踪狂”，她会去参观电视剧和电影的取景地。

1028
00:45:34.600 --> 00:45:35.220
All right.
好吧。

1029
00:45:35.360 --> 00:45:36.220
She went here.
她去了那里。

1030
00:45:36.540 --> 00:45:36.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1031
00:45:37.120 --> 00:45:39.980
She got all kinds of pictures of the restaurant.
她拍了各种各样的餐厅照片。

1032
00:45:40.160 --> 00:45:50.720
She said the owner was so nice and told her that the reason the office picked this restaurant was because there was a big parking lot next door for all the production vehicles.
她说老板人很好，告诉她剧组之所以选这家餐厅，是因为隔壁有个大停车场，可以停放所有的制作车辆。

1033
00:45:50.780 --> 00:45:51.580
That sounds right.
听起来很有道理。

1034
00:45:51.580 --> 00:45:54.300
Yeah, that that's why they got picked.
是啊，这就是他们被选中的原因。

1035
00:45:54.820 --> 00:45:59.280
Shortly after Michael leaves, Dwight and Erin and Holly show up.
迈克尔离开后不久，德怀特、艾琳和霍莉就到了。

1036
00:46:00.020 --> 00:46:01.060
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1037
00:46:01.260 --> 00:46:03.680
They see Michael's photo hanging on the wall.
他们看到了挂在墙上的迈克尔的照片。

1038
00:46:03.840 --> 00:46:05.880
He's holding a little sign that says, Thief.
他手里拿着一个小牌子，上面写着“小偷”。

1039
00:46:06.400 --> 00:46:13.540
Go to 16 Minutes, you guys, because you are going to see a lot of familiar faces, or at least a lot of familiar faces for us, I guess.
大家快去看16分钟处，因为你们会看到很多熟悉的面孔，或者说，对我们来说很熟悉的面孔。

1040
00:46:13.540 --> 00:46:19.040
We had a fan catch from Cessia Z in London, Ontario, Canada.
我们收到了一位来自加拿大安大略省伦敦市的粉丝塞西娅·Z的发现。

1041
00:46:19.040 --> 00:46:23.100
Who noticed that you can see Creed's picture on the wall?
她注意到墙上能看到克里德的照片。

1042
00:46:23.580 --> 00:46:30.800
But if you look to the picture on the left, it looks like there is another picture of Creed with a black wig on, and he's smiling.
但如果你看左边的照片，看起来还有另一张克里德戴着黑色假发的照片，而且他在笑。

1043
00:46:31.020 --> 00:46:32.220
I found this hilarious.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

1044
00:46:32.980 --> 00:46:36.500
Then we had a fan question from Amy D in Kirkland, Washington.
然后我们收到了华盛顿州柯克兰市艾米·D的提问。

1045
00:46:36.580 --> 00:46:39.060
Who were the people in the Thief pictures?
那些“小偷”照片里的人是谁？

1046
00:46:39.380 --> 00:46:40.520
And Jessica N.
还有来自纽约州罗切斯特市的杰西卡·N。

1047
00:46:40.720 --> 00:46:44.560
from Rochester, New York, wants to know if any of them are crew members.
想知道他们中间是否有剧组成员。

1048
00:46:45.100 --> 00:46:46.320
Yes, you guys.
是的，各位。

1049
00:46:47.300 --> 00:46:49.580
I spotted Kelly Cantley.
我认出了凯莉·坎特利。

1050
00:46:49.740 --> 00:46:51.520
She's in the top row, third one over.
她在顶排，从左往右数第三个。

1051
00:46:51.760 --> 00:46:51.960
Yep.
没错。

1052
00:46:52.260 --> 00:46:54.340
I spotted Laverne, our makeup artiSt.
我看到了我们的化妆师拉弗恩。

1053
00:46:54.460 --> 00:46:54.540
Right.
对。

1054
00:46:54.540 --> 00:46:55.540
She was next to Creed.
她就在克里德旁边。

1055
00:46:55.700 --> 00:46:55.880
Yep.
没错。

1056
00:46:56.260 --> 00:46:57.380
That's who I noticed.
我注意到的就是她。

1057
00:46:57.500 --> 00:47:01.760
I had a hard time seeing the pictures clearly.
我很难看清那些照片。

1058
00:47:01.760 --> 00:47:02.660
It's so quickly.
闪得太快了。

1059
00:47:03.020 --> 00:47:07.380
And I tried to even take a picture of it and, like, zoom in, but then it got blurry.
我还试着拍了张照，想放大看看，结果变得很模糊。

1060
00:47:07.560 --> 00:47:08.200
So, I don't know.
所以，我也不确定。

1061
00:47:08.280 --> 00:47:09.380
Did you notice anyone else?
你还注意到其他人了吗？

1062
00:47:09.600 --> 00:47:13.620
I thought I saw Brian Whittle, but, again, it went by so quickly.
我以为我看到了布莱恩·惠特尔，但还是那句话，闪得太快了。

1063
00:47:13.620 --> 00:47:16.660
But Laverne gets a nice, big, like, featured shot.
不过拉弗恩确实有个很棒的大特写镜头。

1064
00:47:16.760 --> 00:47:17.380
She does, yes.
确实，没错。

1065
00:47:18.180 --> 00:47:21.720
I really want to give a shout out to Ben Wang, who played the Chinese restaurant waiter.
我真的想特别提一下本·王，他饰演了中餐馆的服务员。

1066
00:47:21.960 --> 00:47:27.580
He has been in Legion, Fresh Off the Boat, Law & Order and Law & Order SVU.
他曾出演过《大群》、《初来乍到》、《法律与秩序》以及《法律与秩序：特殊受害者》。

1067
00:47:27.760 --> 00:47:28.180
Hey.
嘿。

1068
00:47:28.400 --> 00:47:30.040
You know I love a Law & Order alum.
你知道我最喜欢《法律与秩序》的校友了。

1069
00:47:30.540 --> 00:47:31.640
Ben was really awesome.
本真的很棒。

1070
00:47:32.120 --> 00:47:35.220
Back at the office, nobody is using Gabe's sticky quips.
回到办公室，没人用盖博的便利贴。

1071
00:47:35.320 --> 00:47:37.700
They're not doing the caption contest that he wanted.
他们没在玩他想要的那个配文大赛。

1072
